raphy background when organization provides retirement plan its employees these benefits can become commitment members schemes plan long term economic well being defined benefit plans have potential implications employers terms obligations need met other types plans such defined contribution plans do not guarantee access retirement plan quality benefits thus type plan chosen implications both employees employers conversely properly funded pension plan can help attract maintain employees support long term financial strategic planning part employer guidance defined benefit plans defined contribution plans other types retirement benefits gri economic performance disclosure financial assistance received government reporting organization report following information compilation requirements requirements total monetary value financial assistance received organization any government during reporting period including tax relief tax credits i subsidies investment grants research development grants other relevant types grant iii awards iv royalty holidays v financial assistance export credit agencies ecas vi financial incentives vii other financial benefits received receivable any government any operation viii information country whether extent which any government present shareholding structure c when compiling information specified disclosure reporting organization identify monetary value financial assistance received government through consistent application generally accepted accounting principles background disclosure provides measure governments’ contributions organization significant financial assistance received government comparison taxes paid can useful developing balanced picture transactions between organization government reference bibliography guidance gri economic performance,"['can include', 'organization can', 'economic value', 'reporting organization', 'risk opportunity']","['economic disclosures', 'governments contributions', 'direct income', 'provide econo