ompilation requirements requirements total weight waste directed disposal metric tons breakdown total composition waste total weight hazardous waste directed disposal metric tons breakdown total following disposal operations incineration energy recovery i incineration energy recovery landfilling iii other disposal operations iv total weight non hazardous waste directed disposal metric tons breakdown total following disposal operations incineration energy recovery i incineration energy recovery landfilling iii other disposal operations iv c each disposal operation listed disclosures c breakdown total weight metric tons hazardous waste non hazardous waste directed disposal onsite i offsite d contextual information necessary understand data how data been compiled when compiling information specified disclosure reporting organization exclude effluent unless required national legislation reported under total waste use kilograms measure metric ton background disposal least preferable option waste management hierarchy because its negative impacts environment human health leachate landfills can contaminate land water methane released decay organic waste landfills contributes climate change uncontrolled burning waste contributes air pollution disposal prevents materials present waste being recirculated environment economy making them unavailable future use guidance disclosure templates how present information under disclosure can found tables guidance disclosure when reporting composition waste organization can describe guidance disclosures c besides incineration landfilling organization can specify other types disposal guidance type waste such hazardous waste non hazardous waste waste streams relevant its sector activities tailings organization mining sector electronic waste organization consumer electronics sector food waste organization agriculture hospitality sector materials are present waste biomass metals non metallic minerals plastics textiles gri waste operations it