ples icp measuring fair value securities lending collateral assets fn 550a description approach managing capital liquidity related risks associated systemic non insurance activities entity describe how it manages capital liquidity related risks associated entity ’s engagement systemic non insurance activities systemic non insurance activities are defined investment funding other capital market activities result maturity liquidity transformation leverage imperfect transfer credit risk such repurchase agreements securities lending writing derivatives contracts are not used hedge risk do not closely match underlying exposure sustainability accounting standard insurance scope disclosure include activities all parts entity ’s insurance group including non insurance entities regulated unregulated partly owned entities discussion include entity ’s risk management policy adopted attain compliance regulatory frameworks well voluntarily industry practice entity ’s stress testing well contingency planning stressed situations entity ’s liquidity responsiveness sudden market movements responsiveness entity ’s enterprise risk management erm framework risk management policy change result both internal external events liquidity risk arising changes value liquidity collateral received securities lending activities investment collateral other illiquid assets mark market changes value underlying instrument collateral calls derivatives contracts how entity manages its potential exposure centrally cleared non centrally cleared derivatives sustainability accounting standard insurance,"['esg factors', 'entity describe', 'standard insurance', 'sustainability accounting', 'accounting standard']","['disclosure sustainability', 'incorporates esg', 'disclose policyholder', 'insurance disclosure', 'involving policyholders']","disclosure sustainability, incorporates esg, disclose policyholder, insurance disclosure, involving policyholders, esg factors, entity describe, standard insurance, sustai